§§ `Expressions the index does not list, and expressions with several rows`

-- An expression the index does not list: the index is silent, which does not say the expression is undefined.
#ASSERT `sch 8 the provisions that define or explain the expression` "binder" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 8 the provisions that define or explain the expression` "" EQUALS NOTHING
-- An expression listed only with its scope in the heading: asked without the scope, it is found through the printed form; the wrong scope is not.
#ASSERT `sch 8 the provisions that define or explain the expression` "accounting standards (in Part 16)" EQUALS NOTHING
-- Lines 19635-19637: "address" has two rows.
#ASSERT `sch 8 the provisions that define or explain the expression` "address" EQUALS JUST (LIST "generally in the Companies Acts: section 1142", "in the company communications provisions: section 1148(1)")
-- Lines 19647-19649: "appropriate rate of interest" has two rows.
#ASSERT `sch 8 the provisions that define or explain the expression` "appropriate rate of interest" EQUALS JUST (LIST "in Chapter 5 of Part 17: section 592", "in Chapter 6 of Part 17: section 609")
-- Lines 19719-19724: "director" has five rows.
#ASSERT `sch 8 the provisions that define or explain the expression` "director" EQUALS JUST (LIST "generally in the Companies Acts: section 250", "in Chapter 8 of Part 10: section 240(3)", "in Chapter 1 of Part 11: section 260(5)", "in Chapter 2 of Part 11: section 265(7)", "in Part 14: section 379(1)")
-- Line 19777: "holding company" points at section 1159 and, in the same cell, at section 1160 and Schedule 6.
#ASSERT `sch 8 the provisions that define or explain the expression` "holding company" EQUALS JUST (LIST "section 1159 (and see section 1160 and Schedule 6)")
-- Line 19849: "parent undertaking" points at section 1162 and Schedule 7.
#ASSERT `sch 8 the provisions that define or explain the expression` "parent undertaking" EQUALS JUST (LIST "section 1162 (and see Schedule 7)")
-- Lines 19742-19745: "electronic form, electronic copy, electronic means" has three rows with scope; asked by the printed head "electronic form, electronic copy, electronic means".
#ASSERT `sch 8 the provisions that define or explain the expression` "electronic form, electronic copy, electronic means" EQUALS JUST (LIST "generally in the Companies Acts: section 1168(3) and (4)", "in relation to communications to a company: Part 3 of Schedule 4", "in relation to communications by a company: Part 3 of Schedule 5")
-- Lines 19771-19774: "hard copy form and hard copy".
#ASSERT `sch 8 the provisions that define or explain the expression` "hard copy form and hard copy" EQUALS JUST (LIST "generally in the Companies Acts: section 1168(2)", "in relation to communications to a company: Part 2 of Schedule 4", "in relation to communications by a company: Part 2 of Schedule 5")
-- Lines 19983-19988: "voting rights" (the two rows that point at Schedules 6 and 7).
#ASSERT `sch 8 test the lookup lists` "voting rights" "in section 1159 and Schedule 6: paragraph 2 of Schedule 6"
#ASSERT `sch 8 test the lookup lists` "voting rights" "in section 1162 and Schedule 7: paragraph 2 of Schedule 7"
-- Lines 19681-19690: "company" has eight rows; the dots row at 19685 stands for a repealed row and does not end the group, so the five dash rows after it are scopes of "company".
#ASSERT `sch 8 the provisions that define or explain the expression` "company" EQUALS JUST (LIST "generally in the Companies Acts: section 1", "in Chapter 7 of Part 17: section 616(1)", "in Chapter A1 of Part 25: section 859A(7)", "in Part 26: section 895(2)", "in Schedule 1C (see Chapter 1 of Part 28): paragraph 21 of Schedule 1C", "in Part 26A: section 901A(4)", "in Chapter 3 of Part 28: section 991(1)", "in the company communications provisions: section 1148(1)")
-- The old stand-alone readings are gone: "— in Part 26" is not an expression of the index.
#ASSERT `sch 8 the provisions that define or explain the expression` "— in Part 26" EQUALS NOTHING
-- Line 19992: communication by a company by means of a website is Part 4 of Schedule 5.
#ASSERT `sch 8 test the lookup lists` "website, communication by a company by means of" "Part 4 of Schedule 5"

-- 432 assertions written
